// tests/kernel/drivers/elaborator/mmio_effect_without_cap.pdx — R29-M2-002 (#1024)
//
// Negative fixture: a driver-shaped function that claims `!{Mmio}` in
// its effect row but withholds `paideia.mmio` from its `@{...}`
// declaration. Owner issue #1024 (R29.M2-002 elaborator witness).
//
// This fixture is INTENTIONALLY REJECTED by paideia-as (>= v0.21.0).
// It exists to prove that the elaborator's effect_cap_coupling walker
// (paideia-as#1307, crates/paideia-as-elaborator/src/effect_cap_
// coupling.rs) refuses malformed driver signatures as R29's
// structural witness demands — per
// `design/roadmap/next-wave-softarch.md` §3 R29 — Structural witness:
// every driver process' effect row is checked at link time; a driver
// claiming `!{mmio_read}` without holding an `MmioMemCap` fails
// elaboration.
//
// Verification harness:
//   tools/verify-elaborator-negatives.sh
// invokes `paideia-as build --emit placeholder` on this file and
// asserts exit != 0 AND stderr contains `C1301`. Wired into the
// pre-push matrix as the `elaborator-negatives` step (per
// .githooks/pre-push).
//
// The positive companion at
//   tests/kernel/drivers/elaborator/mmio_effect_with_cap.pdx
// is the same driver shape but declares `@{paideia.mmio}` correctly;
// the verifier asserts that fixture builds clean (exit 0, no C1301).
//
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// What this fixture PROVES
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// (a) The paideia-as pinned via tools/paideia-as at HEAD implements
//     effect-row → cap-set coupling as an elaboration-time check.
// (b) A driver misdeclaration (effect claimed, cap withheld) is
//     rejected with a specific diagnostic code (C1301) naming the
//     missing cap.
// (c) Future R29+ drivers that touch MMIO must therefore hold
//     `paideia.mmio` or elaboration halts before any bytes are
//     emitted — the R29 structural witness is enforceable, not
//     documentation-only.
//
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// What this fixture does NOT prove
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
//   - PAX-manifest link-time re-check (R29.M6+): the same coupling
//     will also be verified at PAX load time against the driver
//     process' cap manifest, so a hand-forged .pax that bypasses the
//     elaborator cannot claim `!{Mmio}` without holding the cap. That
//     landing is a separate milestone.
//   - Op-level enforcement inside handlers: `with handle Mmio { ...
//     perform Mmio::mmio_read(addr) ... }` cases require deeper walker
//     work (effect-handler dispatch), tracked under future R29
//     milestones. Root-effect coverage (RawMem / Mmio family) is what
//     R29.M2-002 delivers.
//
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Fingerprint dictionary
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// This fixture emits NO runtime fingerprint — the witness is purely a
// build-time elaborator negative. `.githooks/pre-push` invokes the
// verify script which asserts the exit code + stderr content.

module MmioEffectWithoutCap = structure {
  effect Mmio {
    op mmio_read : (u32) -> u64
  }

  // driver_bad: intentionally misdeclared — claims !{Mmio} effect
  // in its row but leaves @{} empty. Elaboration must fail with
  // C1301 naming `paideia.mmio` as the missing capability.
  let driver_bad : (u32) -> u64 !{Mmio} @{} =
    fn (addr : u32) -> perform Mmio::mmio_read(addr)
}
